#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:2 39356860755048ffaf6ac952ac941f9b
msgid "_`What this library does not do`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:4 d4b994f1e96d45f394080aa5c4f43f51
msgid ""
"Every row below is a limit that will cost somebody a day if they meet it "
"in the field instead of here. The point of the page is not humility: a "
"control library whose boundaries are unstated gets used outside them, and"
" the failure then looks like a bug in the library rather than a fact "
"about the domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:8 25cebaf9a3e4413899d8510ad0d5e680
msgid ""
"This page is about what the *library* cannot do. It is a different list "
"from :ref:`honest limits <honest-limits>`, which is about what software "
"verification cannot reach and is deferred to hardware -- dead-time, ADC "
"timing, EMI, ISR worst case. Both are needed: one is a property of the "
"method, the other of the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:12 b3515a3720b94a9f8ab00721a0240c6f
msgid ""
"Each row names the case that **pins** it, and the `boundaries` gate "
"checks that every named case still exists. A statement whose case was "
"renamed or deleted therefore fails the build rather than quietly becoming"
" folklore. That is the only reason this page can be trusted after the "
"person who wrote it has moved on."
msgstr ""

