msgid "What it cannot do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:21 ac8a4f528e3f4e868f8dc773792ad12b
msgid "What that means for you"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:22 7341775f1c6047d3afa1de8b0ce518cd
msgid "Pinned by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:23 80f0421faf564aff808fd67d8c172eed
msgid "**Resolve the magnet polarity.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:24 98a16c601a2c41a8b07793fe46811fb4
msgid ""
"The injection observer converges to `dtheta = pi` as happily as to zero: "
"the d axis is right and the magnet is backwards, so the torque sign is "
"inverted. Telling them apart needs a separate pulse or saturation test, "
"which is `MagnetPolarityTest` applied once at commissioning -- not "
"something the observer does for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:27 801a3e25a394457e8f5f4b602964bf38
msgid "``SilHfi.OutsideTheHalfTurnWindowItLocksToTheMirror``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:28 e2c409cd3b2247a680e584cdf8b1a9e2
msgid "**Survive a wrong saliency sign.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:29 eb0702a3b2174ce7ac9981e242f75008
msgid ""
"A machine with `Ld > Lq` needs `demod_gain_a` positive; the wrong sign "
"does not give a worse estimate, it drives the estimate to the unstable "
"equilibrium at `+-pi/2` and leaves it there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:31 1496bf61acd24efc914cf726659481d6
msgid "``SilHfi.AWrongSaliencyDirectionRunsAwayInsteadOfLocking``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:32 541d3ace45d94c3abb99a429879b0ba1
msgid "**Say \"I do not know\" through `ObsState`.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:33 04d5a53e3e0048f896085b731df9f8d2
msgid ""
"The angle has no validity channel. An observer that is not measuring "
"holds its last angle and reports zero speed -- indistinguishable from a "
"stopped machine by those two numbers alone. Use `locked()` (or "
"`status()[\"observer_locked\"]` from Python) to tell them apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:36 0a3847957f78463692bafd091e6e01f7
msgid "``SwitchableObserver.TheSelectedObserversLockVerdictIsReachableThroughTheSlot``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:37 48ce4d37803f470ca310bcf0c0093b1d
msgid "**Run an injection carrier the control rate cannot resolve.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:38 eba33f3247534968972b91f893144b97
msgid ""
"Past `hfi_max_inject_hz(control_hz)` the observer stops: the demodulated "
"amplitude collapses, the lock drops out, the angle freezes, the speed "
"reads zero, and a loop closing on it runs away (measured: -19.5 rad/s of "
"speed bias). The request is refused at setup, and by `update()` for the "
"paths that do not go through the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:41 8e41813863304fd99a2a4f809703f733
msgid "``HfiObserver.ACarrierThisControlRateCannotResolveIsRefusedNotFrozen``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:42 ecec74fdd66b434a87db54d3808990d9
msgid "**Use one carrier frequency at every control rate.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:43 5bc8e314e85147cfb6a4c3dc09796387
msgid ""
"The ceiling is a sampling fact, not a machine fact: 9200 Hz is refused at"
" 20 kHz and accepted at 40 kHz. Sizing a carrier for one rate and reusing"
" it at another is the mistake this row exists to prevent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:45 db784f05bff24d7d8e9702793ceea452
msgid "``HfiObserver.TheCarrierCeilingScalesWithTheControlRate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:46 fbde6209d66f47899bbc0859b3c7b68c
msgid "**Run the injection observer on a surface machine.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:47 98f9e2391c15411a98132d555072c132
msgid ""
"`predicted_gain_a()` is proportional to `(lq - ld)`, so with `lq == ld` "
"the demodulated signal is identically zero and no follower can lock. The "
"mode is refused rather than admitted and left to fail later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:49 43aac89513b84d8ba06a6991c8c5a55e
msgid "``ApiObserverSelector.TheHfiModeRefusesWithoutACarrierOrWithoutSaliency``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:50 5285aa0bc7d042f58416a288731b4a0e
msgid "**Acquire a rotor that is already turning.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:51 77f9d42f89d346ca9c5457ad0e046225
msgid ""
"The loop pulls the angle only inside `+-pi/2` and has no way to pull a "
"frequency it has never seen. A rotor handed to it mid-spin either gets "
"caught or lands on the mirror, and which one is a property of the speed. "
"A hand-over must seed it (`seed_angle`), which is what the blending "
"observer does while the carrier is wound down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:54 e1dfcbfc856648c6a9e70f81d27aeb9d
msgid "``SilHfiEnvelope.AcquiringARotorAlreadyRunningNeedsASeed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:55 c11b3219de1e4b0dae1640606fecb70e
msgid "**Reduce the low-speed servo's residual ripple by improving the angle.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:56 c6d0534331204c989b7a7b5280ca3f64
msgid ""
"The steady bias at 20 rad/s is 0.0039 rad/s (0.02 %); what remains is a "
"ripple at the carrier frequency, and it is the injected current cross-"
"coupling into torque on a turning machine -- linear in `inject_v` and in "
"speed, indifferent to the saliency. Improving the angle by 13x does not "
"move it. `inject_v` is the knob."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:59 1f7a3a05c7444f30b27303089bd43a23
msgid "``SilSpeedRipple.TheFigureSurvivesSubstepResolution``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:60 d7d6a27dc2634123b014f56df3f708dd
msgid "**Reconstruct what the hardware actually did from a trace.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:61 c2b78087415d4815b3a23238b4e3dff9
msgid ""
"The trace records what the loop *believed*: the currents the PI acted on "
"and the voltages it applied before modulation. A trace that looks perfect"
" is therefore entirely consistent with a miscalibrated current sensor -- "
"the loop is faithful to a wrong measurement. Use it to explain the loop's"
" decisions, not to measure the phases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:64 6c836d844597401ebacbc031cd0ba59c
msgid "``Trace.TheRecordAgreesWithTheScalarReadBitForBit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:65 d199d40c134741e5bc1f35b05c4b4e52
msgid "**Start a load the drive cannot move.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:66 2fca9f33b0804c12b14c6f16b6279366
msgid ""
"The sequence ramps to its limit, holds, and after its grace period "
"reports `Failed` with zero torque: measured 0.200 N*m at 0.5 N*m/s "
"reached at 400 ms, then a 200 ms grace. It cannot conjure torque -- the "
"only honest answers are \"released\" and \"cannot start\", and from "
"outside a silent axis is indistinguishable from a working one, which is "
"why the failure is a state rather than an absence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:70 67651cb62eb7483bb7735de97d09dd7c
msgid "``StallStart.AStuckAxisSaysFailedInsteadOfRampingForever``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:71 ee0f6a1045fa4a4b90481070620cc52a
msgid "**See a fault code while the drive is derating.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:72 3c7ee46c02c54f618fd76d10ffae9016
msgid ""
"A hot machine below the trip temperature reports `fault = None` and "
"`active_mask = 0` while its current limit is already falling -- measured:"
" 3.00 A at 45 C, 1.80 A at 80 C, both with output allowed, then 0 A and "
"no output at 105 C. `output_allowed` is defined as `active_mask == 0`, so"
" a fault means \"authority removed\" and derating is not one: read "
"`i_limit_a` against the `i_max_a` you configured if you want to know the "
"machine is hot. A commissioning tool that shows only the fault code will "
"report a derating drive as healthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:77 dc9f8455777d4802b43ef649b46455a6
msgid "``Protection.TheTemperatureLadderIsGradedRatherThanACliff``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:78 b2738834e9474b3aa39b21cd57c9c3ad
msgid "**Estimate a torque that accounts for iron loss or magnet temperature.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:79 44b7112a97884a88b28ca1e6d42da3ec
msgid ""
"`torque_estimate()` is `kt*iq + 1.5*pp*(ld-lq)*id*iq`, and `kt` is a "
"nameplate number: it does not know that the magnet weakens as it heats, "
"that iron loss subtracts torque at speed, or that the inverter adds no "
"torque. The 5 % agreement it reports is against the same model the plant "
"integrates, so it is an agreement about the *model*, not a claim about a "
"hot machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:83 9ff566c7bb244255b5285effca7c5598
msgid "``TorqueMap.TheEstimateMatchesTheMechanicsOfTheSilBench``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:84 98e6ca6fb3a94024a49cbee12f9fed05
msgid "**Improve a sensored axis's angle by adding the carrier.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:85 580ca7a62d6c4b6a9c017c2d75f438df
msgid ""
"The sensor owns the commutation angle, so the injection observer now runs"
" for its own demodulation only: the carrier does reach the inverter "
"(measured swing 0.45--0.67 across eight rate/PWM combinations), but the "
"sensor keeps the angle and the published speed. `status()[\"observer\"]` "
"naming `HFI` therefore does *not* mean the loop is commutating on the "
"injected estimate -- compare the two explicitly if that is what you need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:89 086d737ae6df480186fa9ca4b1827298
msgid "``MotorInjection.ASensoredAxisInjectsWithoutSurrenderingTheAngle``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:90 c8e70b77062340de94d67989c74d0897
msgid "**Get a quiet speed estimate out of the injection observer for free.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:91 b3c7e6960ef949aeb7442e97eeeeb146
msgid ""
"`omega_e = omega_int + kp*error`, and `error` carries the carrier, so the"
" published speed holds 0.4180 rad/s at 2000 Hz in a 20 rad/s servo unless"
" `speed_lpf_hz` is set. The library's own path sets it (200 Hz); a caller"
" that constructs the observer directly gets the raw value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:94 f9bf4c8077204288afbb85dd1ec4f6a1
msgid "``SilSpeedRipple.ThePublishedSpeedCanBeCleanedAndTheRotorDoesNotCare``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:95 14ecf9e282d04c4aab2c523b8c2ce38c
msgid "**Close a servo on a ten-millisecond-old speed.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:96 9283127a7bed4c45b59ea5e8096927c3
msgid ""
"Differencing the angle is quieter than the PLL and worse in a loop: at a "
"200 rad/s speed-loop bandwidth the window is transport delay in the "
"feedback path, and no window length from 500 us to 10 ms wins on both "
"settled accuracy and peak. The route is closed by measurement, not by "
"taste."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:99 7276776c40b3407c830305fd8ffcbccd
msgid "``SilSpeedFromAngleClosedLoop.AWindowShortEnoughToBeOnTimeIsTheOnlyWayThisRouteWins``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:100 6b4137dde0b04b99b7026f7643d2df59
msgid "**Get a rotor angle out of three Hall sensors alone.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:101 7bc3f07c41b447c8b131cb85122eac14
msgid ""
"The code carries 60 degrees of information per edge and *nothing* inside "
"a sector: two angles 59.96 degrees apart read the same code, so a decoder"
" that sees only the code is wrong by up to 30 degrees -- worst case, half"
" a sector, and no cleverness improves it. Ten degrees of mounting error "
"on one sensor widens the bound to 35 and narrows the other sectors to 25 "
"without ever producing an illegal code, so misplacement is invisible to "
"the wiring. Everything finer than 60 degrees has to come from edge "
"*timing*, which is the decoder's work, not the sensor's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:107 3135aece711445e6b994cc7eb45dd3d0
msgid "``HallPhysics.InsideOneSectorTheCodeCarriesNoAngleInformation``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:108 785a6caed8cd440fa74946c6aa9889e1
msgid "**See a dead Hall sensor all the time.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:109 41c9fa09af3c434fa4224dfb34808333
msgid ""
"A stuck sensor freezes its bit: one sixth of a revolution reads as the "
"illegal code 0 or 7 (that is the entire visible fault) and the other five"
" sixths read as perfectly legal codes at 120-degree resolution, with the "
"edge interval doubled. Worse, every surviving transition still flips "
"exactly one bit, so the adjacency check that most decoders carry never "
"fires -- measured, not assumed, and the first version of that case "
"asserted the opposite. Anything built on Halls must watch the illegal "
"window *and* the edge timing; either alone has a blind spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:114 f2eb40557ff0482fa8e153b43edf7dbc
msgid "``HallPhysics.ADeadSensorIsSilentForFiveSixthsOfTheRevolutionAndKeepsEveryRemainingCodeLegal``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:115 e9ce593958b44e2692ca9052c9600914
msgid "**Declare a dead Hall sensor over the whole revolution.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:116 728fccb699df4384ac2ddbfa8927ff93
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Both channels together still leave **8.4 % of a revolution reading `Ok` "
"while wrong by up to 59 degrees** (13.7 % and 120 degrees with the sensor"
" stuck high): the illegal window is 15.5 % and the interval check another"
" 53.9 %, so roughly a third of every revolution is undeclared. A drive "
"built on Halls needs a second opinion -- current or torque sanity, an "
"index, anything independent of the codes -- rather than a cleverer check "
"on the codes. This is the number that decides how the fault has to be "
"handled, and it is asserted so it cannot quietly become \"the fault is "
"caught\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:122 4a06b42aa46a4da9852406e9923fef46
msgid "``HallTracker.AStuckSensorIsCoveredByTwoChannelsAndNeitherAloneIsEnough``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:123 a9b369760cbb4e4ebfc4885acf4c18e6
msgid "**Cancel friction you have not measured.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:124 c9350ac08b384f35a7553c4b2736f3eb
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The compensation is a torque of its own, so an estimate above the "
"machine's breakaway moves the rotor even when the reference is held still"
" -- measured, **5.625 mrad of travel with no command at all** from a "
"`(0.030, 0.030)` estimate on a machine whose breakaway is 0.020. Below "
"the breakaway it is safe but it takes the residual with it: `(static - "
"coulomb)/kp` follows the estimate wherever it goes, 2.021 mrad at the "
"true value and 1.007 at a 50 % over-estimate. There is nothing in the "
"code stream that can tell you the estimate is wrong -- it has to come "
"from a measurement, and the boundary of \"good enough\" is the breakaway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:130 68ccfdc0f2bd4c7f9e8b843bfd9b97b7
msgid "``FrictionComp.AnEstimateAboveTheBreakawayWalksTheAxisWithNoCommandAtAll``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:131 9e7bf7fc521f4f31a7e02ea6c50dfafb
msgid "**Tell a stalled axis from a friction estimate that is too low.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:132 d9d54e3f04a84210ad6c3d5938ce661d
msgid ""
"Both read as \"at rest while the loop asks for more than the estimate\", "
"which is exactly what `stalled` reports, so the flag is honest about "
"being one fact and not a diagnosis. Distinguishing them needs a second "
"signal -- a torque measurement, an encoder that is not moving, or a "
"command that would obviously move a healthy axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:135 24c482cb1a82463cb278a4e3a394bf81
msgid "``FrictionComp.TheStallFlagNeedsBothStillnessAndADemandAboveTheBreakaway``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:136 ab1c59affecc410f98c192d82117f935
msgid "**Stop an axis at a wall without knowing the drive's delay.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:137 02bfa156191c4d24839304be29f37ebd
msgid ""
"The velocity ceiling is `v^2 <= 2*a*(d - v*dt)` and `dt` is the drive's "
"own latency, not the control period: on the SIL axis it is about 1 ms "
"(one period plus the 0.8 ms current rise). Assuming it is zero -- the "
"natural reading of \"it can decelerate at `a`\" -- crosses the wall by "
"**19 mm at 20 rad/s**, which is exactly `v*dt`; with it the axis stops "
"**1.04 mm short**. It cannot be derived from anything in the library, so "
"it has to come from a commissioning run or a datasheet, and the number "
"passed in should be the conservative one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:142 9eda6d4782c34f529bda271e4a3cff43
msgid "``SoftLimit.TheDelayTermIsTheDifferenceBetweenNineteenMillimetresPastAndOneShort``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:143 7ff9a496bc08423ebf5aa1be39dc3de2
msgid "**Synchronise two axes with a position-only gear.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:144 762ddf2cc2e54e659c941a86edb57f39
msgid ""
"A perfectly geared pair still shows a standing error of `v*kd/kp` -- "
"**25.6 mrad** at 10 rad/s with `kd` 0.02 and `kp` 8 -- because a position"
" loop following a moving reference always lags it. It scales with the "
"rate and inversely with the gain, so raising `kp` buys accuracy at the "
"price of stability, and the only term that removes it is the gear's "
"velocity output fed forward as `+kd*v_ref`. A gear that emits only a "
"position is a lag generator with a ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:149 299b77c64dac427998a8a7cae008b3d3
msgid "``ElectronicGear.TheSyncErrorIsTheRampLagInBothOfItsTerms``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:150 96b753cbfd1e42bd8e9543e72ffe15d0
msgid "**Trust `v_max / psi_f` for the top speed.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:151 872db7009ece4f999cc2ee70b021b00a
msgid ""
"It over-promises by about 4 %: the d-axis drop `we*Lq*iq` is part of the "
"bus too. At 24 V and this nameplate the naive ceiling is **2910 rad/s "
"electrical** and the machine's own steady state reaches **2794**, and "
"weakening by `id = -2 A` lifts it to **3320** -- a factor of **1.188**, "
"not the 1.202 the flux ratio promises, because the weakening current's "
"own d-axis voltage eats part of the margin it buys. Both numbers come "
"from bisecting the voltage that holds the operating point, not from a "
"datasheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:156 db152ad2acbf4f99833a9020046fdcd9
msgid "``HighSpeed.TheVoltageCeilingIsFourPercentBelowTheNaiveRatioAndWeakeningLiftsIt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:157 2354c2b317d8429b835e23691cd1383d
msgid ""
"**Read the open-loop flux observer's angle at speed without knowing its "
"bias.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:158 948374daf5fe433782d6afce0080167f
msgid ""
"Seeded and fed correctly it still carries a **0.12 rad mean error at 200 "
"rad/s electrical and 0.08 at 600** -- a bias, not a sampling effect, "
"which is why it is not speed-proportional and why the number has to be "
"measured for the machine in front of you rather than assumed small. What "
"*is* speed-independent at a fixed samples-per-cycle ratio and degrades "
"4.7x when the ratio drops from 40 to 8 is the sampling error on top of "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:162 e99c7c1e59184aa3b886b3d923139be3
msgid "``HighSpeed.TheErrorFollowsSamplesPerCycleRatherThanTheSpeed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/boundaries.rst:164 ca469e29649043749ff480c9b863eaa9
msgid ""
"What is *not* on this page, because it is enforced by a gate rather than "
"by a test case: no exceptions, no RTTI, no `new`/`delete`, no "
"`std::vector`/`std::string`, C++17 and C11 only (`strict`), every "
"installed header carrying a README claim row (`claims`), and every number"
" in the documentation matching an artefact the build produced (`docs`)."
msgstr ""

